    "notes": "The complete principal palace includes both returned wings, its projecting roof halls and five gold onion domes. A pale tapered chapel pavilion connects the five drums to the roof. The east facade keeps its three rows of layered windows, pilasters and simplified gilded trim. The local grade, ornament, roof joints and chapel masonry are visualization approximations. The detached forecourt ranges, Lyceum link, Cameron gallery, pavilions and park use the host map. The review covers the principal palace exterior."
